- (5) Populations of endangered or threatened species, or habitat for such species; and

- (6) Archaeological sites, cemeteries and burial grounds.

- (c) The following are considered Secondary Conservation Areas and should be included within the open space to the maximum extent feasible:

- (1) — Important historic sites;

- (2) Existing healthy, native forests with a contiguous area of at least one (1) acre;

- (3) Individual existing healthy trees greater than eight (8) inches caliper, as measured five (5) feet high from ground level on the bole of the tree (diameter breast high);

